1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Section 3

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,703
NATALIE:

3
00:00:02,703 --> 00:00:07,617
Dave, I'm worried about our case study, I've done a bit of reading,

4
00:00:07,617 --> 00:00:11,508
but I'm not sure what's involved in actually writing a case study - I

5
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:15,700
missed the lecture where Dr Baker talked us through it.

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,583
DAVE:

7
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:18,709
OK, well it's quite straightforward.

8
00:00:18,709 --> 00:00:24,004
We've got our focus - that's tourism at the Horton Castle site.

9
00:00:24,004 --> 00:00:28,400
And you said you'd done some reading about it.

10
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:28,813
NATALIE:

11
00:00:28,813 --> 00:00:33,770
Yes, I found some articles and made notes of the main points.

12
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:34,096
DAVE:

13
00:00:34,096 --> 00:00:38,660
Did you remember to keep a record of where you got the information from?

14
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:38,984
NATALIE:

15
00:00:38,984 --> 00:00:39,308
Sure.

16
00:00:39,308 --> 00:00:42,870
I know what a pain it is when you forget that.

17
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:43,300
DAVE:

18
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:43,730
OK,

19
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:46,740
so we can compare what we've read.

20
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:52,760
Then we have to decide on a particular problem or need at our site.

21
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:58,350
And then think about who we're going to interview to get more information.

22
00:00:58,350 --> 00:00:58,864
NATALIE:

23
00:00:58,864 --> 00:00:59,379
OK.

24
00:00:59,379 --> 00:01:01,437
So who'd that be?

25
00:01:01,437 --> 00:01:04,009
The people who work there?

26
00:01:04,009 --> 00:01:07,610
And presumably some of the tourists too?

27
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:08,031
DAVE:

28
00:01:08,031 --> 00:01:09,713
Yes, both those groups.

29
00:01:09,713 --> 00:01:15,181
So we'll have to go to the site to do that, I suppose.

30
00:01:15,181 --> 00:01:20,650
But we might also do some of our interviewing away from the site -

31
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:26,539
we could even contact some people here in the city, like administrators involved in

32
00:01:26,539 --> 00:01:27,380
overseeing tourism.

33
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:27,792
NATALIE:

34
00:01:27,792 --> 00:01:28,204
OK.

35
00:01:28,204 --> 00:01:33,145
So we'll need to think about our interview questions and fix times

36
00:01:33,145 --> 00:01:35,204
and places for the meetings.

37
00:01:35,204 --> 00:01:38,910
It's all going to take a lot of time.

38
00:01:38,910 --> 00:01:39,309
DAVE:

39
00:01:39,309 --> 00:01:39,707
Mmm.

40
00:01:39,707 --> 00:01:45,286
And if we can, we should ask our interviewees if they can bring along

41
00:01:45,286 --> 00:01:49,670
some numerical data that we can add to support our findings.

42
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:50,410
NATALIE:

43
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:51,890
And photographs?

44
00:01:51,890 --> 00:01:52,293
DAVE:

45
00:01:52,293 --> 00:01:55,514
I think we have plenty of those already.

46
00:01:55,514 --> 00:02:01,152
But Dr Baker also said we have to establish with our interviewees whether we

47
00:02:01,152 --> 00:02:06,790
can identify them in our case study or whether they want to be anonymous.

48
00:02:06,790 --> 00:02:07,207
NATALIE:

49
00:02:07,207 --> 00:02:10,547
Oh, I wouldn 't have thought of that.

50
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:16,390
OK, once we've got all this information, I suppose we have to analyse it.

51
00:02:16,390 --> 00:02:16,848
DAVE:

52
00:02:16,848 --> 00:02:23,267
Yes, put it all together and choose what's relevant to the problem we're focusing

53
00:02:23,267 --> 00:02:23,725
on,

54
00:02:23,725 --> 00:02:29,685
and analyse that carefully to find out if we can identify any trends

55
00:02:29,685 --> 00:02:31,060
or regularities there.

56
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:36,692
That's the main thing at this stage, rather than concentrating on details

57
00:02:36,692 --> 00:02:38,570
or lots of facts.

58
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:39,092
NATALIE:

59
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:39,614
OK.

60
00:02:39,614 --> 00:02:43,790
And then once we've analysed that, what next?

61
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:44,186
DAVE:

62
00:02:44,186 --> 00:02:49,335
Well , then we need to think about what we do with the data

63
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:54,088
we've selected to make it as clear as possible to our readers.

64
00:02:54,088 --> 00:02:55,276
Things like graphs,

65
00:02:55,276 --> 00:02:56,068
or tables,

66
00:02:56,068 --> 00:02:56,860
or charts ...

67
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:57,635
NATALIE:

68
00:02:57,635 --> 00:02:58,410
Right.

69
00:02:58,410 --> 00:02:58,808
DAVE:

70
00:02:58,808 --> 00:03:02,391
Then the case study itself is mostly quite standard;

71
00:03:02,391 --> 00:03:04,780
we begin by presenting the problem,

72
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:08,761
and giving some background, then go through the main sections,

73
00:03:08,761 --> 00:03:14,334
but the thing that surprised me is that in a normal report we'd end

74
00:03:14,334 --> 00:03:19,111
with some suggestions to deal with the problem or need we identified,

75
00:03:19,111 --> 00:03:23,490
but in a case study we end up with a question

76
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:29,064
or a series of questions to our readers and they decide what ought to

77
00:03:29,064 --> 00:03:29,860
be done.

78
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:30,445
NATALIE:

79
00:03:30,445 --> 00:03:33,370
Oh I hadn't realised that.

80
00:03:33,370 --> 00:03:33,813
NATALIE:

81
00:03:33,813 --> 00:03:41,342
So basically, the problem we're addressing in our case study of the Horton Castle site is why

82
00:03:41,342 --> 00:03:44,000
so few tourists are visiting it.

83
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,045
And we'll find out more from our interviews,

84
00:03:47,045 --> 00:03:53,135
but I did find one report on the internet that suggested that one reason might be

85
00:03:53,135 --> 00:03:56,560
because as far as transport goes, access is difficult.

86
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:56,971
DAVE:

87
00:03:56,971 --> 00:03:58,617
I read that too,

88
00:03:58,617 --> 00:04:02,321
but that report was actually written ten years ago,

89
00:04:02,321 --> 00:04:05,201
when the road there was really bad,

90
00:04:05,201 --> 00:04:07,259
but that's been improved now.

91
00:04:07,259 --> 00:04:13,019
And I think there's plenty of fascinating stuff there for a really good day

92
00:04:13,019 --> 00:04:13,431
out,

93
00:04:13,431 --> 00:04:18,780
but you'd never realise it from the castle website - maybe that's the problem .

94
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:19,336
NATALIE:

95
00:04:19,336 --> 00:04:22,670
Yes, it's really dry and boring.

96
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:23,045
DAVE:

97
00:04:23,045 --> 00:04:28,289
I read somewhere a suggestion that what the castle needs is a visitor centre.

98
00:04:28,289 --> 00:04:33,533
So we could have a look for some information about that on the internet.

99
00:04:33,533 --> 00:04:35,780
What would we need to know?

100
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:36,151
NATALIE:

101
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:36,523
Well,

102
00:04:36,523 --> 00:04:38,750
who'd use it for a start.

103
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:44,319
It'd be good to know what categories the visitors fell into too, like school parties

104
00:04:44,319 --> 00:04:45,433
or retired people,

105
00:04:45,433 --> 00:04:50,260
but I think we'd have to talk to staff to get that information .

106
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:50,648
DAVE:

107
00:04:50,648 --> 00:04:51,037
OK.

108
00:04:51,037 --> 00:04:56,472
And as we're thinking of suggesting a visitor centre we'd also have to look

109
00:04:56,472 --> 00:04:57,637
at potential problems.

110
00:04:57,637 --> 00:05:01,520
I mean, obviously it wouldn't be cheap to set up.

111
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:01,892
NATALIE:

112
00:05:01,892 --> 00:05:02,265
No,

113
00:05:02,265 --> 00:05:05,243
but it could be a really good investment.

114
00:05:05,243 --> 00:05:10,456
And as it's on a historical site it'd need to get special planning permission.

115
00:05:10,456 --> 00:05:11,201
I expect.

116
00:05:11,201 --> 00:05:12,690
That might be hard.

117
00:05:12,690 --> 00:05:13,035
DAVE:

118
00:05:13,035 --> 00:05:17,862
Right, especially as the only possible place for it would be at the entrance ,

119
00:05:17,862 --> 00:05:20,620
and that's right in front of the castle.

120
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,240
NATALIE:

121
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:21,860
Mmm.

122
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:22,200
DAVE:

123
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:26,286
But it could be a good thing for the town of Horton.

124
00:05:26,286 --> 00:05:29,350
At present it's a bit of a ghost town.

125
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:34,648
Once they've left school and got any skills or qualifications, the young people all

126
00:05:34,648 --> 00:05:39,567
get out as fast as they can to get jobs in the city,

127
00:05:39,567 --> 00:05:43,730
and the only people left are children and those who've retired.

128
00:05:43,730 --> 00:05:44,162
NATALIE:

129
00:05:44,162 --> 00:05:44,593
Right.

130
00:05:44,593 --> 00:05:50,636
Something else we could investigate would be the potential damage that tourists might cause

131
00:05:50,636 --> 00:05:54,520
to the castle site, I mean their environmental impact.

132
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:59,038
At present the tourists can just wander round wherever they want,

133
00:05:59,038 --> 00:06:04,789
but if numbers increase, there might have to be some restrictions, like sticking to

134
00:06:04,789 --> 00:06:05,610
marked ways.

135
00:06:05,610 --> 00:06:10,510
And there'd need to be guides and wardens around to make sure these were

136
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:10,860
enforced.

137
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:11,505
DAVE:

138
00:06:11,505 --> 00:06:16,020
Yes, we could look at that too.

139
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:17,310
OK, well ...
